\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Software validation contract for the affine fast path. Left: analytical multiplication and addition counts compare the affine rule with one-step wrapped-Gaussian references. Middle: Q4.20 software fixed-point emulation shows small p99 correction differences and no observed residual-boundary crossing-rate change in the controlled sample set. Right: software-in-the-loop runtime counters make overflow and fast-cycle violations visible under the current protocol. The figure summarizes data-backed software checks; it is not FPGA synthesis, timing closure, power/resource measurement, source-vs-board agreement or board commit latency evidence.}}{21}{figure.caption.35}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:validation-contract}{{3}{21}{Software validation contract for the affine fast path. Left: analytical multiplication and addition counts compare the affine rule with one-step wrapped-Gaussian references. Middle: Q4.20 software fixed-point emulation shows small p99 correction differences and no observed residual-boundary crossing-rate change in the controlled sample set. Right: software-in-the-loop runtime counters make overflow and fast-cycle violations visible under the current protocol. The figure summarizes data-backed software checks; it is not FPGA synthesis, timing closure, power/resource measurement, source-vs-board agreement or board commit latency evidence}{figure.caption.35}{}}
